# Kirara Server Software License Agreement

> Version v1.9 | Last updated: October 2, 2026

**IMPORTANT NOTICE:** This License Agreement (the "Agreement") is a legal agreement between you and the Kirara Server Development Team concerning your use of the Kirara Server software (the "Software"). Before installing, copying, or using the Software, please read all terms of this Agreement carefully, in particular the provisions concerning disclaimers, limitation of liability, user data and privacy, and system permissions. By clicking the "Agree" button, installing, or otherwise using the Software, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by all terms of this Agreement. If you do not agree, please do not install or use the Software.

## Article 1 Definitions

1.1 **The Software** means the Kirara Server APP, including all of its components, modules, built-in Schemes, interfaces, icons, documentation, explanatory materials, and all updates, patches, and upgrade packages provided by the Developer, regardless of the form in which they are delivered (installer package, archive, or source code). The Software also includes built-in modules such as the App Store, Download Manager, Notification Center, and Community interaction.

1.2 **Services** means the various remote services accessed after creating an "Instance" in the Software and binding a "Scheme" to it, including but not limited to media playback (Kirara Media), live streaming (Kirara Live), cloud storage (Kirara Team Shared Cloud), email (Kmail), team collaboration (Chat), virtualization platforms (Vmm/ESXi), remote desktop (Winserver series), OpenVPN virtual private network, and others, as actually made available within the Software.

1.3 **Server** means the Kirara Server cloud platform operated by the Developer, which provides services such as account authentication, template distribution, comment storage, notification push, feed cards, Scheme configuration synchronization, avatar and background assets, and cloud sync.

1.4 **User** means the natural person or legal entity that installs and uses the Software, i.e., the contracting party to this Agreement. **Developer** means the Kirara Server Development Team and its authorized entities. **Content** means data that you create, upload, manage, or access through the Software, including instance configurations, token information, comments, files, and media.

1.5 **Instance and Scheme**: An Instance means a configuration unit you create in the Software, which is divided into "User Instances" (for your day-to-day use of specific applications) and "Service Instances" (for you to maintain Kirara Server–related services). A Scheme means the functional template bound to an Instance (such as media playback Kirara Media, live streaming Kirara Live, cloud storage, email Kmail, team collaboration Chat, virtualization platforms Vmm/ESXi, remote desktop Winserver series, OpenVPN virtual private network, game server resource platform, etc.). The Schemes actually available are those made available within the Software and delivered by the Server.

1.6 **App Store and Plugins**: The App Store means the built-in entry point in the Software for browsing, searching, and downloading ecosystem resources and for installing and uninstalling plugins. **Plugins** means third-party components and extension Schemes that you obtain through the App Store or other channels and install on your local machine or in the Software's directory.

1.7 **Cloud Sync** means the function provided by the Software that uploads a "Token Package" or "Instance Package" to the Server in end-to-end encrypted form and allows you to download and restore it at any time.

1.8 **Community Content** means content that you submit through the Software and that may be visible to other users, including comments, replies, likes, @ mentions, homepage shares, favorite records, update-request messages, nicknames, and avatars.

1.9 **Download Manager** means the feature in the Software that centrally displays download tasks and supports pausing, resuming, stopping, and opening the containing folder. Files downloaded through the Download Manager, web download takeover, application updates, and software update installers are written to the system download directory or a designated update directory.

## Article 2 Grant of License

2.1 Subject to your compliance with all terms of this Agreement, the Developer grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, revocable personal-use license permitting you to install, copy, and use the Software on devices you own. The license term begins at the time the Software is installed and ends on the date this Agreement is terminated.

2.2 This license does not include any right to access, modify, or distribute the Software's source code, unless such rights are separately granted by an applicable open-source license (such as the MIT License). The main body of the Software's code is released as open source under the MIT License, and the rights you enjoy under that license are not restricted by this Agreement; however, the services you connect to through the Software, the server resources you access, and the non-open-source portions of the Software (including certain Scheme adaptation logic, the encrypted cache mechanism, plugin installation and privilege-elevation logic, and the server communication protocol) remain subject to this Agreement and the corresponding terms of service.

2.3 The Software may include or link to third-party open-source components and programs (such as OpenVPN, FreeRDP, and WebView2) and permits you to install third-party plugins from the App Store. Your use of such components and plugins is also subject to their own licenses and terms of service. In the event of a conflict between this Agreement and a third-party license, this Agreement shall be interpreted in a manner that does not deprive you of the rights granted by that third-party license.

2.4 Except for the rights expressly granted by this Agreement, the Developer reserves all rights in and to the Software and its derivative works (including copyright, trademark rights, patent rights, and other intellectual property rights). Any rights not expressly granted to you under this Agreement are deemed reserved by the Developer.

2.5 The rights in third-party plugins, App Store resources, and the trademarks, logos, and content contained therein belong to their respective providers. Your downloading, installation, and use of such content are also subject to the licenses and terms of service of their providers, and this Agreement does not alter the rights granted to you by such licenses and terms.

## Article 3 Usage Restrictions

3.1 You may not rent, lend, sell, or resell the Software or its Instances, tokens, or Schemes, or use them for commercial operation or service hosting for others, except with the Developer's written permission.

3.2 You may not decompile, disassemble, reverse engineer, crack, or bypass the license verification of the Software, or attempt to extract its source code, except in cases of compatibility interoperability expressly permitted by applicable law. You may not delete, alter, or obscure any copyright notices, trademark logos, or license information in the Software.

3.3 You may not use the Software to engage in any activity that violates the laws and regulations of the People's Republic of China or the laws of your jurisdiction, including but not limited to: unauthorized access to the systems and data of others, network attacks and penetration, distribution of malicious programs or harmful code, infringement of the intellectual property or privacy rights of others, sending spam, and circumventing service access controls.

3.4 The Software provides an auto-login (token link) function, which may be used only for accounts and services you are entitled to access. You may not use this function to mass-acquire the credentials of others, to gain unauthorized access, or to engage in any form of account abuse. You bear all consequences arising from improper use.

3.5 Cloud Sync is intended solely for the backup and restoration of your own data. You may not use Cloud Sync to upload unlawful or harmful content, to upload data you have no right to dispose of, to upload another person's export package to your own cloud space, or to use the function to circumvent storage limits or attack the server.

3.6 The token QR-code export and import function uses a server-side one-time session key negotiation mechanism, and the session key is issued only to the token's rightful owner. You may not bypass this mechanism in any way to obtain, decrypt, or use another person's token, and you may not replay, tamper with, or mass-capture QR-code frames.

3.7 You may not bypass or defeat the Software's plugin installation verification, privilege-elevation execution flow, path security validation, or global mutex control, and you may not compromise the integrity of the Software or affect other users by tampering with the application directory, system services, the registry, or installed components.

3.8 **Community Content Rules:** Content you submit through comments, replies, @ mentions, homepage shares, update requests, nicknames, avatars, and the like must be truthful, lawful, and must not infringe the rights of others. You may not post information that is unlawful or non-compliant, pornographic or violent, defamatory or insulting, harassing to others, spam advertising, or fraudulent or deceptive. Update-request messages must first select the corresponding media library, and the content must not exceed 500 characters. The Developer has the right, without prior notice, to delete or block non-compliant content, or to restrict the community functions of the relevant account.

## Article 4 User Data and Privacy

4.1 **Local Data:** The Software stores data such as instance configurations, Scheme bindings, tokens, comments, notification records, and application settings locally on your device, in the "Kirara" folder under the system user data directory (%APPDATA%/Kirara). The local database is a single-file embedded database (LiteDB). When the Software is uninstalled, this folder is retained by default; you may delete it manually to remove it completely.

4.2 **Encryption Protection:** Sensitive fields in tokens (account name, account password, API key, server address) and login credentials (RefreshToken) are stored using AES-256-GCM encryption, with the encryption key protected by Windows DPAPI (current-user scope). Resources cached from the Server, such as background images, avatars, template covers, Scheme icons, and .ovpn configurations, are also stored in an encrypted cache to prevent tampering. Please safeguard your Windows account and login credentials. The Developer is not liable for leakage caused by another person's access to your login session or to unencrypted copies.

4.3 **Server Communication:** To enable functions such as account authentication (login/registration/auto-login), template retrieval, comment synchronization, notification push (SignalR real-time push), feed cards, incremental Scheme URL synchronization, avatar and background asset downloads, and OpenVPN configuration distribution, the Software communicates with the Server and transmits the necessary account identifier, session token, local version number, and content you actively submit. Apart from the necessary scenarios described above, the Software will not upload your local data without your action.

4.4 **Third-Party Service Data:** The services you connect to through each Scheme (such as media libraries, cloud drives, and mailboxes) are independently operated by their respective service providers. Your data therein is governed by their terms of service and privacy policies and is unrelated to the Software and the Developer.

4.5 **Data Directory and Account Isolation:** The Software stores local data in physically isolated locations per logged-in account — each account's data is located in the "Kirara" folder under the system user data directory (%APPDATA%/Kirara/users/account identifier), which contains the local database (the single-file embedded database LiteDB), encryption keys, credential files, and various resource caches. There is also a global layer (%APPDATA%/Kirara/global) that stores account-independent infrastructure configuration, homepage backgrounds, and login history, as well as a browser data directory (%LOCALAPPDATA%/Kirara/users/account identifier/webview2).

4.6 **Cloud Sync Data:** What Cloud Sync uploads is an AES-256-GCM encrypted package derived from an identifier of your own. The Server performs only per-user isolated key-value storage and metadata registration, and never decrypts or parses the logic inside the package. Server synchronization stores data in an overwriting manner, keeping only the latest copy per user per type and retaining no historical versions. You may delete your cloud data in the Software at any time. The Developer is not liable for access to or loss of synchronized data caused by leakage of your own account credentials or by failure of the cloud storage service.

4.7 **Visibility of Community Content:** Community content that you actively submit, such as comments, replies, likes, homepage shares, update-request messages, nicknames, and avatars, will be stored on the Server and may be displayed to other users and administrators or used for interactive notification push. @ mentions will send a notification to the mentioned user. Please do not submit personal information or sensitive data in Community Content that you do not wish others to know.

4.8 **Logs and Diagnostic Information:** The Software generates local runtime logs, crash logs, and auto-login diagnostic logs (such as crash.log and autologin_debug.log in the Kirara data directory) for troubleshooting purposes. Such logs do not record plaintext passwords or token ciphertext. If you need to report a problem to the Developer, please review the log contents yourself before providing them.

4.9 **Data Export, Import, and Complete Erasure:** You may export and import encrypted data packages through the data management function (including instances, tokens, software setting preferences, and Notification Center service items; the license agreement consent flag and feed cards are not included in the export). The export package contains sensitive credentials — please keep it safe. Losses caused by leakage of the export package are borne by you. You may also completely remove local data through "Clear Data" (clearing account data and all local caches), "Clear Cache" (clearing only browser data), or by checking the option to clear data during uninstallation. These operations are irreversible; please back up in advance.

## Article 5 Network Services and Third-Party Services

5.1 **Network Dependency:** Online functions such as account authentication, template retrieval, comment synchronization, notification push, and configuration synchronization depend on an Internet connection and Server availability. Network interruptions, carrier failures, server maintenance, or force majeure may render such functions unavailable or delayed. The Developer does not guarantee that online services will be provided continuously and without interruption, and is not liable for losses arising therefrom.

5.2 **Independence of Third-Party Services:** The third-party services targeted by each Scheme (media, cloud drives, mailboxes, virtualization platforms, etc.) are independently provided and maintained by their operators. The Developer is not liable for their content, availability, stability, security, or their handling of your data. When using third-party services, you should review and comply with their terms of service and privacy policies.

5.3 **Compliance of Remote Connections:** When using remote connection functions such as OpenVPN, please ensure that your conduct complies with the management rules of the network you are connecting to and with applicable law. Some countries or regions may impose legal restrictions on the use of virtual private networks; you should verify the relevant legality yourself and bear the corresponding responsibility. Network conditions, server-side configuration, and carrier policies may all affect connection quality; the Developer does not guarantee that connections will be stable, successful, or achieve any particular speed.

5.4 **App Store and Third-Party Plugins:** The ecosystem resources, plugins, and extension Schemes in the App Store are uploaded and maintained by the Developer or by third-party providers. Plugins may run as separate processes, require administrator privileges, or modify local files and system components; their functionality, security, compatibility, and legality are the responsibility of their providers, and the Developer is not liable for the content or behavior of third-party plugins. Please confirm that the source is trustworthy before installing. System abnormalities, data loss, security incidents, or legal disputes caused by installing or using third-party plugins shall be resolved between you and the plugin provider. The Developer has the right to delist, block, or remove App Store content.

5.5 **Feed and Remote Content:** Homepage feed cards (image, video, and HTML types) are delivered by the Server, and their content is the responsibility of the publisher. The Developer is not liable for the accuracy or legality of third-party published content. Please do not interact with interactive elements within a card unless you have confirmed that it is safe.

5.6 **Aggregation Management Platform:** Accounts with administrator or super-administrator privileges may access a web-based management console through the Software to manage users, Scheme URLs, notifications, templates, feeds, and downloadable resources. Management operations directly affect all users; please strictly comply with the Developer's management rules. Consequences arising from exceeding authority, abusing management privileges, or misoperation are borne by the operator.

## Article 6 System Permissions and Security

6.1 **Permission Description:** Installing the Software and its components may require administrator privileges, in order to register system services (KiraraVpnHelper, which launches OpenVPN on behalf of the application under the LocalSystem identity), install/load virtual network adapter drivers (TAP/Wintun), and write to the Program Files directory. In addition, the Software supports a persistent system tray icon, writes a startup entry to the registry according to your settings (the Run key under HKEY_CURRENT_USER), and installs or uninstalls third-party plugins through an elevation flow in the App Store. The above permissions are used only to the extent necessary for the Software's normal functions.

6.2 **Channel Security:** Please obtain the Software and its updates only from the Developer's official channels (the official website, officially released installers, and official update channels). The Developer assumes no responsibility for installers, cracked versions, or modified versions of unknown origin, and such versions may contain malicious code, steal your credentials, or compromise system security.

6.3 **Security Obligations:** You bear full security responsibility for your account credentials (username, password, API key, token, and RefreshToken) and for access rights to the services you manage, including but not limited to setting strong passwords, not disclosing credentials to others, logging out promptly, and enabling auto-login protection on public devices. Losses caused by credential leakage, data theft, or service abuse resulting from your failure to safeguard them are borne by you.

6.4 **Vulnerability Reporting:** If you discover a security vulnerability or defect in the Software, you are welcome to report it through the channels published by the Developer. Please do not publicly disclose vulnerability details or exploit the vulnerability to attack the systems of others before the Developer has fixed it.

6.5 **QR Codes and Session Credentials:** The QR code generated by token QR-code export contains encrypted token data, and anyone who obtains that QR code may import the token through the official client. Please display the QR code in a private environment and avoid screenshots, recordings, forwarding, or prolonged public display. The QR-code import session has a validity period, after which it must be regenerated.

