## Article 10 Termination

10.1 If you breach any term of this Agreement, the Developer has the right to terminate this license by written notice to you, without incurring any liability. Upon termination of this license, you shall immediately stop using the Software and uninstall and delete all copies.

10.2 You may terminate this Agreement at any time by uninstalling the Software. Uninstallation deletes only the program files in the installation directory and system components (including registered system services); your local data (the %APPDATA%/Kirara directory) is retained by default, and you must delete that directory manually to remove it completely.

10.3 Upon termination of this Agreement, the provisions of Articles 2 through 13 that by their nature should survive (including but not limited to disclaimers, limitation of liability, intellectual property, governing law, and dispute resolution) shall remain in effect.

10.4 Termination of this Agreement does not affect the rules governing the handling of Community Content you have already uploaded to the Server. You may delete your Community Content within the Software, and Cloud Sync data may be deleted within the Software at any time. If you wish to deregister your account or request deletion of account-related data, please contact the Developer through the official channels it publishes.

## Article 11 Changes to the Agreement

11.1 The Developer may update this Agreement from time to time to reflect changes in product features or legal requirements. The updated Agreement will be published within the Software and marked with a version number and effective date. For material changes (such as significant adjustments to the scope of the license, data processing methods, or the scope of system permissions), the Developer will, to the extent possible, notify you through in-Software notifications and may require you to re-read and agree before you may continue to create instances or use the relevant functions.

11.2 After an updated Agreement takes effect, your continued installation or use of the Software or acceptance of the relevant services constitutes your having read and accepted the updated Agreement. If you do not agree to the changes, you should stop using the Software and uninstall it.

## Article 12 Governing Law and Dispute Resolution

12.1 The formation, validity, interpretation, performance, and dispute resolution of this Agreement shall be governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China (excluding conflict-of-law rules). Where this Agreement references third-party licenses (such as the MIT License), the governing provisions of those licenses shall prevail for those parts.

12.2 Any dispute arising out of or relating to this Agreement shall first be resolved by the parties through friendly negotiation. If negotiation fails, either party may bring a lawsuit before the people's court with jurisdiction at the Developer's place of domicile. During the litigation, the remaining provisions of this Agreement shall continue to be performed, except for the matters in dispute.

## Article 13 Miscellaneous

13.1 **Severability:** If any provision of this Agreement is held invalid or unenforceable by a court or competent authority of jurisdiction, that provision shall be modified or severed to the minimum extent permitted by law, and the validity of the remaining provisions shall not be affected.

13.2 **Entire Agreement:** This Agreement (together with other policies and announcements published within the Software) constitutes the entire agreement between you and the Developer regarding the use of the Software and supersedes any prior oral or written agreements between the parties concerning the Software.

13.3 **Waiver:** The Developer's failure to exercise or delay in exercising any right under this Agreement shall not constitute a waiver of that right, and any single or partial exercise shall not preclude any other or further exercise.

13.4 **Contact:** If you have any questions about this Agreement or the Software, you may contact the Developer through the official channels it publishes. The last-updated date of this Agreement shall be as published within the Software.

13.5 **Record and Withdrawal of Consent:** Your consent status to this Agreement is recorded locally on a per-logged-in-account basis. The Settings Center provides a "Withdraw License Agreement" entry; upon withdrawal, the Software will close immediately. After withdrawal, you must re-read and agree to this Agreement before you may continue to create User Instances or Service Instances.

